From 4889fbdbf439ac2a2a51009dca531f1110e49d41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartheek Palla <palla.kartheekreddy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 22:34:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(oid4vc-service): publish the issuer's own display
 metadata

Needed by wallet-driven issuance, and separate from the authorization_code
work, so it is its own commit rather than folded into the port.

A wallet that lists issuers has nothing but the credential issuer's
`display` to label the entry. Without it the citizen is asked to choose
'98.70.36.106.sslip.io' instead of 'National Identity Authority' - which
is the exact step the charter describes as 'the citizen selects the
National Identity Authority'. The service published display per credential
configuration but never for the issuer itself.

ISSUER_DISPLAY_NAME, ISSUER_DISPLAY_LOGO_URI and ISSUER_DISPLAY_LOCALE,
all optional. An unset name omits `display` altogether rather than
publishing an empty one: absent lets a wallet fall back to something of
its own choosing, while blank looks deliberate.

Writing the test twice was instructive - the first attempt invented a
constructor signature and a default export that do not exist. It now uses
the same harness shape as the existing specs and reads configuration the
way the service does, from the environment at construction.

12 suites / 131 tests pass.
